        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="MAC19" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Ange-Denis</forename>
                        <surname>Macquin / Makin</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1756-10-16">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1823-07-17"/>
                    <occupation>Antiqarian, author</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Mackin is most likely a mispelling on Godwin's part of the historian and
                            author Ange-Denis Maquin. Educated in Meaux he moved to England in 1792,
                            he met Godwin numerous times between 1798 and 1809, although his name
                            was spelt many different ways following these encounters. Following this
                            move he published on a wide range of subjects from gastronomy to
                            religion. It is noted in the DNB that he was a staunch critic of the
                            French Revolution, only returning to France after the fall of Napoleon.
                            Godwin does not record his death in 1623. In total, his name is spelt by
                            Godwin as Mackin and McQuin, as well as the correct version. </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"></bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title> DNB, National Archives, Ed Pope</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
